# Identity layer

The single source of truth for the operator's identity, project parameters, working style, and execution rules is located statically at `../THE-NEXUS/01-USER-DATA/IDENTITY.md`.

Read and parse this file to harvest:

- **Section 1. TECHNICAL TOPOLOGY & ROLE** - role, stack, infrastructure footprint, downstream consumers, production loop
- **Section 2. PIPELINE & WORKFLOW MECHANICS** - tools, initialization path, validation engine, definition of done
- **Section 3. QUALITY CRITERIA & STANDARDS** - senior-level execution bar and documentation signals
- **Section 4. NEGATIVE CONSTRAINTS** - anti-patterns, banned phrases, failure modes to avoid
- **Section 5. SYSTEM EXECUTION DIRECTIVES** - numbered enforceable rules governing AI behavior in active sessions

Do not infer identity from memory or stale chat context when this file resolves. Treat `# USER_IDENTITY_BLOCK` as the schema anchor.

## Pacing signals (don't miss these)

- Asking follow-up questions = stay on the topic.
- Short confirmations ("ok", "go", "next") = next step.
- "Slow down" or "one thing at a time" = you firehose'd; reset.

## When you hand off to another AI

Use `../THE-NEXUS/06-WORKFLOWS/ai-orchestra-handoffs.md`. Always include the four-part packet: pointer to current state, pointer to plan, precise ask, success criteria.
